      "content": "\n# 🌐 My Networking Journey — From Fundamentals to Practical Experience\n\nI started learning computer networking from the fundamentals and gradually moved toward practical configuration and troubleshooting.\n\n### 📚 1. Networking Fundamentals\n- Network types and topologies\n- OSI & TCP/IP models\n- Network devices\n- Transmission media\n- Ethernet and RJ45\n\n### 🔢 2. IPv4 Addressing\n- IPv4 structure\n- Network vs host portions\n- Subnet masks\n- Public & private IPv4\n- Loopback and link-local addresses\n- Classful vs classless addressing (CIDR)\n\n### 🔀 3. Routing & Network Communication\n- Default gateways\n- Routing concepts\n- Routing to the Internet\n- NAT (Network Address Translation)\n- Broadcast and directed broadcast\n- Understanding how packets move between networks\n\n### 🔧 4. Cisco Configuration\n- Cisco IOS basics\n- Switch configuration\n- VLANs & Access ports\n- Trunk concepts\n- Router configuration\n- Basic network troubleshooting\n\n### 🖥️ 5. Cisco Packet Tracer\nI moved from theory to practice by creating and configuring network topologies, connecting devices, assigning IP addresses, configuring VLANs and testing connectivity.\n\n### 🧪 6. Real Troubleshooting Practice\nI also practiced using Windows networking commands such as:\n\n```powershell\nipconfig\nping\n```\nand connectivity testing between local gateways and Internet addresses.\n\n### 🎓 7. Certification & Continuous Learning\nThis journey has included Cisco networking coursework, practical Packet Tracer exercises, networking training, and certification-focused learning.\n\nThe biggest lesson has been that networking is not only about memorizing commands — it is about understanding **how devices, addresses, routes and packets work together.**\n\nStill learning. Still practicing. 🌐🚀\n\n`#Networking` `#Cisco` `#CCNA` `#PacketTracer` `#IPv4` `#Routing` `#VLAN` `#NAT` `#NetworkEngineering` `#ITStudent`\n",
